# Every claim a crate marked verified takes without proving it, checked by tools/check-external-body.py
# against the source. external_body exempts a function from the proof of what it does, and the reason
# line beside it says why; exec_allows_no_decreases_clause exempts its loops and calls from the proof
# that they end; assume_specification states the specification of a function Verus does not read,
# and the citation lines above it say who vouches for it (design/who-vouches-for-an-unproven-claim/).
# Fields, separated by tabs: path from the repository root, item, attribute, class, reason; an
# assumed specification's reason is its citation lines' text, joined by '; '.
#
# hardware  an assumed specification in an arch module, citing the manual passages it restates
# kernel    an assumed specification naming the kernel item whose proof it restates
# glue      hardware or assembly leaf glue still spelled external_body, until it is one of the two above
# gap       uses something this Verus cannot check: a raw pointer, a conjured permission, uninit memory,
#           or a ghost of state outside the program that nothing ties to the real one
# unproven  plain code or a lemma with no proof yet, or a wait with no termination proof yet, so proof debt
kernel/verified/arch/aarch64.rs	flush_every_context	assume_specification	hardware	arm-arm C5.5.77 TLBI VMALLE1, TLBI VMALLE1NXS; arm-arm D8.17.8 Ordering and completion of TLB maintenance instructions
kernel/verified/arch/aarch64.rs	load_translation_root	external_body	glue	only the hardware can attest which root a core translates through, so only this changes a BaseRegister
kernel/verified/arch/aarch64.rs	read_producer	external_body	glue	only the SMMU's producer register holds the queue's wrap bit, and its index is the ring's tail since only the invalidate moves either
kernel/verified/arch/aarch64.rs	serial_write_byte	external_body	glue	waits on the PL011's flag register and stores one byte in its data register through memory-mapped registers, which have no state a proof could see
kernel/verified/arch/aarch64.rs	store_command	external_body	glue	the SMMU reads the queue, so only this can say what one of its slots holds
kernel/verified/arch/aarch64.rs	submit_invalidate	external_body	glue	only the SMMU can attest an invalidate, so only this empties its IOTLB model
kernel/verified/arch/x86_64.rs	flush_every_context	assume_specification	hardware	amd-apm2 5.5.1 Process Context Identifier; amd-apm2 5.5.3 TLB Management, Implicit Invalidations; amd-apm2 5.5.3 TLB Management, Caching of Upper Level Translation Table Entries
kernel/verified/arch/x86_64.rs	load_translation_root	external_body	glue	only the hardware can attest which root a core translates through, so only this changes a BaseRegister
kernel/verified/arch/x86_64.rs	serial_write_byte	external_body	glue	waits on COM1's line status and stores one byte in its transmit holding register through port I/O, which has no state a proof could see
kernel/verified/arch/x86_64.rs	store_command	external_body	glue	the IOMMU reads the ring, so only this can say what one of its slots holds
kernel/verified/arch/x86_64.rs	submit_invalidate	external_body	glue	only the IOMMU can attest an invalidate, so only this empties its IOTLB model
kernel/verified/pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_map_take	external_body	glue	clears a hardware page table word and returns it in one atomic exchange, since another core's walk may set the accessed or dirty bit between a read and a write
kernel/verified/pagetable/pagemap_util_t.rs	page_map_take_status	external_body	glue	replaces a hardware page table word with the arch module's without_status of it in a compare-exchange, since another core's walk may set a status bit between a read and a write
kernel/verified/queue_lock.rs	acquire	exec_allows_no_decreases_clause	unproven	the spin waits for the holder to hand over, and bounded overtaking is not yet proven
kernel/verified/queue_lock.rs	release	exec_allows_no_decreases_clause	unproven	the spin waits for the successor to link itself, and bounded overtaking is not yet proven
kernel/verified/queue_lock.rs	spin_hint	external_body	glue	the pause instruction, which has no state a proof could see
aeager/src/glue.rs	page_permission	external_body	gap	conjures the permission to a mapped page's bytes; the map contract puts the frame's page in the space's tables, writable since the frame's capability has the write right, and nothing proves that the calling thread runs in that space, that no other permission covers the page or that the page is memory Rust may read and write
acall/src/step.rs	step	external_body	gap	the system call instruction, whose ensures is what Kernel::dispatch proves of a step that returns to the calling thread, on the premise that the caller token was the kernel's state and the caller's root when the process was handed it and no other step ran since the previous return, which nothing proves
